-# AI-BOT
\ No newline at end of file
+# AI-BOT · DarkDevil Quant
+
+A single-owner **ZebPay research and paper-trading workspace**, built from the exact Postman collection you supplied. React + TypeScript on the frontend; Express + TypeScript on the backend; one origin and one HTTP port.
+
+> **Important:** this is NOT ready for real-money execution. The collection is incomplete for required live safety checks. Live trading is permanently blocked in this implementation, including after explicit opt-in. No outbound exchange POST or DELETE adapter exists. Withdrawals and transfers are not implemented.
+
+The original repository contained only `README.md`; there was no existing application architecture or working trading implementation to preserve.
+
+## What works, and what does not
+
+| Feature                                                    | Collection support / implementation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |
+| ---------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| Secure credential entry                                    | Implemented: owner login, masked write-only inputs, HTTPS/localhost gate, backend AES-256-GCM vault. No credential returned in a response.                                                                                                                              |
+| Read-only connection verification                          | Implemented using signed **Spot `GET /api/v1/orders`**, pending filter. It proves order-read access, not trade permission, account identity, or IP-whitelist configuration.                                                                                             |
+| Spot prices                                                | Implemented from the documented public market list; source, observation time, unavailable states, and 15-second REST polling. The BTC-INR ticker has an independently tested adapter with its exact documented `group=singapore`.                                       |
+| Open/completed Spot orders                                 | Implemented: signed reads, pages of up to 500, actual returned statuses, and read-only reconciliation of a known order ID.                                                                                                                                              |
+| Futures public market data                                 | Implemented: exact-symbol metadata/prices, depth, nested 24-hour ticker, public aggregates, and a separate service-health check. Public trades are not account fills; health does not verify an account. Conflicting ticker percentages and fee units remain unassumed. |
+| Actual INR balances / available funds                      | **Unavailable.** Spot balance requests exist, but no response format is defined. Values are `null`, never fictional balances or assumed zero.                                                                                                                           |
+| Spot fills / TDS / trading fees / trading filters          | **Unavailable.** Request paths exist, but response schemas are absent. No fields or units are guessed.                                                                                                                                                                  |
+| Real cancellation                                          | **Unavailable.** DELETE authentication and response formats are not specified. Cancel existing orders directly in your ZebPay account.                                                                                                                                  |
+| Futures account balances, orders, leverage, positions, P&L | **Disabled.** Futures-specific signing is absent; some request/prose authentication and timestamp rules conflict. No sibling Spot signing is assumed to apply.                                                                                                          |
+| Paper trading                                              | Implemented: virtual INR, long-only Spot market simulations, decimal arithmetic, adverse assumed slippage/fees, manual review, persistent ledger, risk limits, idempotency, and emergency stop. Needs a real available ZebPay quote to fill.                            |
+| Signal research                                            | Implemented: explainable, fixed SMA/RSI rules with rationale and risk, paginated decision journal and complete linked-fill outcomes (including archived virtual wallets), manual ticket prefill only. **Not a trained AI; no automatic learning or optimization.**      |
+| Backtesting                                                | Partial: only genuine **locally recorded Spot observations**. No historical candle endpoint is in the file; no earlier history is invented or fetched elsewhere. Next-observation execution; costs explicitly assumed.                                                  |
+| Live execution                                             | **Blocked.** Missing balance schemas, filters, verified costs/permissions, and cancellation safety prevent activation. Four Spot payload formats and POST signing are tested **offline only**.                                                                          |
+| IP-whitelist/API scope introspection                       | **Unsupported.** The IP field is an explicitly labeled user declaration. The app never claims that the whitelist was API-verified.                                                                                                                                      |
+| Withdrawals / transfers                                    | Deliberately not implemented; no app route or transport method. Configure restricted API-key permissions directly in ZebPay as well.                                                                                                                                    |
+
+Read the full [collection audit](docs/COLLECTION_AUDIT.md), [security notes](docs/SECURITY.md), and [acceptance report](docs/ACCEPTANCE.md) before using account credentials.
+
+## Beginner setup: your own computer
+
+### 1. Install the prerequisites
+
+- Node.js **22.13 or newer** (tested here with 22.22.3); npm is included.
+- Open a terminal in this project folder.
+
+```sh
+npm ci
+```
+
+No ZebPay key or secret belongs in a source file, terminal command, chat message, or frontend environment variable.
+
+### 2. Create your owner password
+
+```sh
+npm run setup
+```
+
+This interactive command asks twice for a **new workspace password** (at least 14 characters). It is **not** your ZebPay API secret. Entry is hidden; only a salted scrypt hash is saved. Setup respects your optional `.env` configuration. Local runtime files have restricted permissions and are ignored by Git.
+
+### 3. Start the app
+
+```sh
+npm run dev
+```
+
+Open `http://localhost:3000` on your own computer. Click the lock icon to unlock with your workspace password.
+
+If the server was already running before setup, **restart it**. An unconfigured server intentionally stays read-only: anyone with a preview URL must not be able to initialize the owner or enter exchange credentials.
+
+The server binds to `0.0.0.0` for hosted previews, but account entry over plain HTTP is permitted **only for localhost development**. A remote deployment requires HTTPS. All browser API calls are relative URLs on the same origin; no browser-to-backend `localhost` URL is hardcoded.
+
+### 4. Configure ZebPay directly
+
+In your ZebPay account, create/review a restricted API key using the exchange's own controls. Keep withdrawal/transfer permissions off. Enable the appropriate supported **read** access.
+
+If IP whitelisting is required, add the **public outbound IP of the backend server**, not your browser's IP or a private LAN address. Obtain that IP from your hosting/network configuration. The collection provides no IP-check or permission-introspection endpoint. This app cannot discover or bypass those restrictions.
+
+### 5. Connect through the secured page
+
+1. Open **ZebPay connection**.
+2. Enter your key and secret in the masked inputs. They are cleared immediately on submission.
+3. Select your **self-reported** server IP-whitelist status.
+4. Click **Connect & verify**.
+5. `Connected` requires a schema-valid, successful signed pending-orders read. `Failed` and `Permission missing` do not grant access or enable trading.
+
+Read verification makes **one** request. It does not test permissions by submitting an order. Restarting or locking the workspace leaves saved credentials unverified until you explicitly verify again. **Disconnect** aborts in-flight account reads and deletes the encrypted credential record; it does **not** cancel existing exchange orders.
+
+### 6. Start with paper trading
+
+- Unlocking reveals the actual local simulated wallet, initialized with **₹1,00,000 of virtual INR**, not an exchange balance.
+- Keep market polling on. No simulation fills without an available, positive INR Spot quote returned by ZebPay.
+- Enter base-asset quantity, review the simulated debit/credit, and explicitly confirm the paper order.
+- Default paper limits: ₹5,000 maximum simulated notional, ₹1,000 daily simulated loss, **assumed** 10 bps fee and 5 bps adverse slippage. These are **not verified ZebPay fees**.
+- Change these in **Risk & safety**. Limits are rechecked on the backend, with fresh valuations and a transaction around ledger updates.
+- A persistent emergency stop blocks simulations before quote lookup and again before commit. Reset requires a separate typed phrase. It never enables live execution or cancels existing exchange orders.
+
+The daily reference is the first fresh valuation of that UTC day (not a reconstructed midnight valuation). Missing prices for any held simulated asset block further simulations and suppress current equity/P&L rather than valuing missing assets at zero.
+
+### 7. Research without autopilot
+
+- At least 20 genuine continuous observations are needed for directional SMA/RSI analysis.
+- At least 40 recorded Spot observations are needed for a backtest — about ten minutes at uninterrupted 15-second sampling.
+- Observations are collected only when the workspace requests them; closing/pausing the UI does not run an unattended market collector.
+- No candle backfill, trained model, automatic strategy improvement, or automatic execution is implemented.
+- **Prefill paper ticket** only fills the side/decision link. It never submits an order.
+
+Backtests use at most the latest 1,000 stored observations, long-only positions, the maximum-order cap, next-observation fills, and explicit cost assumptions. They do not model taxes, liquidity/partial fills, or the paper daily-loss latch. They are exploratory research, not a live-execution safety certification or expected-return promise.
+
+The journal/export is a bounded view: 200 current-wallet fills, 25 decisions per page, 20 recent backtests, and 200 audit events. Decision pages and linked-fill pages (20 per page) are navigable. Each visible decision's summary queries **all** its stored linked fills, including archived wallets; current-wallet performance totals likewise use its entire ledger, not just the displayed 200 fills. A BUY entry has no claimed realized exit result; SELL-fill P&L/rates are recorded simulation results, not round-trip strategy accuracy. The visible export is still not a complete database backup.
+
+The Markets page's Futures section also reads the exact documented `ticker24Hr?symbol=...` and `aggTrade?symbol=...` requests. The saved ticker has inconsistent nested/outer percentage fields; both are shown raw with a conflict warning, never averaged or used as a trading signal. Public aggregates are market-wide and cannot establish an account fill. The optional public-service health check only recognizes the documented `message: OK`; it never changes account connection status. These are REST snapshots, not candles, historical backfill, or a live trade stream.
+
+Exchange pair edits require **Apply pair**, not a signed request on every keystroke.
+
+## Hosting securely
+
+See [SECURITY.md](docs/SECURITY.md) for the full deployment boundary.
+
+1. Run owner setup privately before exposing the app.
+2. Use exactly one trusted HTTPS reverse proxy and a single application instance with persistent private storage.
+3. Supply `DARKDEVIL_MASTER_KEY` through your host's **backend secret manager**: base64 encoding of 32 cryptographically random bytes. Never use a `VITE_` variable, put it in Git, or share it in chat. For an existing data directory, securely reuse its original key — do not silently replace it with a new random key. For a fresh deployment, inject the production key before owner setup.
+4. Supply an exact `DARKDEVIL_PUBLIC_ORIGIN`, such as your own `https://quant.your-domain.example`, without a trailing slash.
+5. Configure `DARKDEVIL_DATA_DIR` to a private persistent directory if needed (default `.runtime`). Do not place it in `public`, `dist`, source folders, or a parent of the app; those locations are rejected. Back it up securely; keep the master key separately.
+6. Permit backend HTTPS egress to the **documented** hosts `www.zebapi.com` and `futuresbe.zebpay.com`. Correct server time is required for millisecond signing.
+7. Build and start:
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+npm start
+```
+
+Production refuses to start without a master key, owner configuration, and exact HTTPS origin. No CORS access is enabled. Disable request-body/header logging and session-replay recording at every reverse proxy/monitoring layer.
+
+**This Arena preview:** no real credentials were provided. Its network policy permits selected package/Git hosts, not the documented exchange hosts. Real authenticated access, account balances, and exchange availability have therefore **not** been verified here. The empty/unavailable state is intentional. Run from your own secured, correctly whitelisted server with exchange egress to perform the supported account-read verification.
+
+## Checks
+
+```sh
+npm test                 # Unit + HTTP integration tests; synthetic test-only transport, no real exchange traffic
+npm run typecheck
+npm run format:check
+npm run build
+npm run check:secrets    # Working-tree safeguard; no credential scanner can prove an arbitrary file is secret-free
+npm run test:coverage
+```
+
+The GitHub safety workflow runs these mocked backend checks, build, and secret safeguard on pushes and pull requests. No real API credentials belong in CI.
+
+Browser tests use explicit **test-only network fixtures**, never a production fallback. Run the app in another terminal before running them:
+
+```sh
+npm run dev
+# In another terminal:
+npm run test:e2e
+```
+
+A headless Linux Chromium is packaged as a dev dependency to avoid third-party browser-download hosts in restricted environments. Other platforms can set `PLAYWRIGHT_EXECUTABLE_PATH` to their own installed Chromium. Browser sandbox flags apply only to the test runner, never the application.
+
+To reproduce the audit from the **same supplied file**:
+
+```sh
+npm run audit:collection -- "/path/to/Zebpay API Documentation.postman_collection(1).json"
+```
+
+The script checks SHA-256 `0462b41646c31a25cc9580b873d91eb57c42072346807e86b7895795f4defdbd`. A different export must be reviewed before changing that pin. The raw collection is deliberately not committed: it includes account-specific example data. The sanitized [JSON audit](docs/collection-audit.json) records all 38 requests, all 30 saved response schemas, and all 58 event definitions, without publishing their account values.
+
+## Project map
+
+```text
+src/                    React interface; no exchange secret/configuration
+shared/                 Safe response types and explicit capabilities
+server/auth.ts          Single-owner session, scrypt authentication, CSRF/origin checks
+server/vault.ts         AES-256-GCM encrypted credential record
+server/zebpay.ts        Pinned GET-only exchange adapter and schema validation
+server/connection.ts    Read-only verification, generation fences, disconnect/abort handling
+server/markets.ts       Public reads/snapshots, exact symbols, bounded receipt-time observations
+server/public-cache.ts  Bounded/coalesced public-only read cache, no automatic retry
+server/journal.ts       Decimal full-ledger outcomes and paper performance, paginated linked fills
+server/paper.ts         Decimal ledger, risk checks, duplicate protection, atomic paper fills
+server/live-safety.ts   Hard live gate; four offline-only Spot payload serializers
+server/research.ts      Fixed explainable rules and next-observation backtests
+server/store.ts         SQLite persistence and credential-free HMAC-linked audit trail
+scripts/                Private interactive owner setup, audit reproduction, secret safeguard
+tests/                  Synthetic transport, unit/integration and browser tests; not deployed client assets
+docs/                   Audit, security model, and honest acceptance status
+.runtime/               Ignored private runtime state; NEVER commit or serve
+```
+
+No withdrawal/transfer code, other-exchange adapter, LLM provider, third-party telemetry, or external chart feed is included.
