+# Acceptance status — not a live-trading certification
+
+## Audit outcome
+
+The original checkout contained only an eight-byte README. A new single-origin React/Express workspace was therefore built rather than claiming to preserve non-existent trading code.
+
+Only the supplied collection was used. All 38 requests, 30 saved responses, and 58 event definitions were inspected. The raw export was not committed because it contains account-specific examples; its SHA-256 and sanitized schemas are pinned in `collection-audit.json`.
+
+## User acceptance checklist
+
+| Requested acceptance criterion                         | Status                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |
+| ------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
+| 1. Credentials entered securely                        | **Implemented and tested locally.** Owner-only, masked write-only fields, HTTPS/localhost gate, CSRF/origin checks, encrypted backend record. No real user credentials were entered here.                                                                                                              |
+| 2. Supported read-only request verifies connection     | **Implemented and tested with a synthetic transport.** Exact documented Spot pending-orders GET and signature; HTTP 200 with an undocumented body does not connect. Actual ZebPay authentication has not been tested here.                                                                             |
+| 3. Actual balances and market data displayed correctly | **Partial / cannot fully pass.** Public Spot/Futures parsers and real-data-only UI are implemented and contract-tested. Real network access is not established here. Spot balance response schemas are absent, so balances remain unavailable. No funds, prices, positions, or profits are fabricated. |
+| 4. Paper works without real orders                     | **Implemented and tested.** Decimal balances/fees, manual review, caps/loss checks, long-only inventory, idempotency/concurrency/restart safety. The paper engine can only perform public market GETs, never private exchange mutations. It needs an actual available quote in normal operation.       |
+| 5. Live disabled until explicitly enabled              | **Passes with stricter behavior.** Paper is the default; explicit acknowledgment/readiness check still cannot enable live, because required safety contracts are missing. No flag overrides this.                                                                                                      |
+| 6. Every live order uses a verified endpoint/format    | **No live orders are allowed or sent.** Four Spot payload formats and POST signing are tested offline, but there is no outbound POST/DELETE transport. Cannot claim a verified live execution.                                                                                                         |
+| 7. Unsupported fields/features clearly identified      | **Implemented.** Detailed UI support matrix, all 38 request findings, nullable unavailable account values, reasoned disabled states. Futures private operations remain off.                                                                                                                            |
+| 8. No secret committed                                 | **No real API credentials were supplied or added.** Runtime data, environment files, raw collection, generated artifacts and logs are ignored; automated safeguards and encryption/nonreflection tests are included. Tests use clearly marked synthetic credentials only.                              |
+
+**Overall:** ready for reviewing the interface, local safety behavior, supported read-only connection code, and paper/research implementation. **Not ready for real-money trading or a claim that all requested acceptance criteria have passed.** Balances/live safety require additional authoritative collection information, not guesses.
+
+## Fully implemented local features
+
+- Secure single-owner setup/login, password hashing, session rotation/expiry, origin/CSRF checks, HTTPS credential gate, no CORS account access.
+- Backend AES-256-GCM credential vault, private runtime files, masked responses, no credential logging/echo, verified-only connection storage.
+- Supported Spot GET signing, typed order reads, actual returned statuses, read-only known-ID reconciliation, abort/generation fencing and disconnect.
+- Public Spot market list and exact-symbol Futures prices/metadata/depth/24-hour ticker/aggregate snapshots, plus a separate public-service health check; no cross-exchange feeds/conversions or fake fallback values.
+- Isolated persistent virtual wallet, decimal market simulations with adverse assumed costs, available virtual funds/inventory checks, maximum-order/daily-loss guards, duplicate request protection, atomic ledger, persistent emergency latch.
+- Deterministic SMA/RSI signals with explanations and limitations, no execution side effects, locally observed-price backtests with next-observation fills and explicit assumptions. Delayed latest-history reads cannot overwrite newly initiated research; non-finite metrics/results fail safely.
+- Paginated owner-only decisions and linked executions across current/archived virtual wallets, complete Decimal ledger aggregation, and current-wallet paper performance. BUY entries have no inferred realized exit attribution. A profitable-SELL-fill percentage is not strategy accuracy or a round-trip win rate.
+- Credential-free HMAC-linked audit events, bounded visible-journal export (not a complete database backup), feature/request audit, beginner setup/security documentation.
+
+## Partial / blocked by the supplied collection
+
+- Real INR and coin balances, available/locked funds: request-only, no Spot response fields.
+- Spot fee/TDS, fills and trading filters: no response contract; cannot safely validate live debit, lot size or price limits.
+- Spot cancellation: no DELETE signature rule or response contract.
+- Spot book: undefined `baseUrl` in both request and original example; no alias repair.
+- Spot live order creation: format documented, required preflight state not documented. Offline-only serializers.
+- Futures wallet/orders/history/linked orders/positions/P&L/margin/leverage/cancellation: private auth is ambiguous or conflicting; disabled.
+
+## Unsupported / deliberately absent
+
+- Historical candles, backfill, API-permission/IP-whitelist introspection, account-identity verification, Bearer token acquisition.
+- Unattended execution, automatic learning, automatic improvement/optimization, external model/provider integration.
+- Futures strategy execution/backtesting, margin/leverage simulation, Spot shorting, limit-order matching.
+- Withdrawals/transfers and any other exchange integration.
+
+## Verification performed
+
+Automated unit and HTTP integration tests use a strict **test-only synthetic fetch transport** with the supplied schemas; they cannot contact a real exchange. Browser fixtures, when used, are also explicitly scoped to tests and never bundled as application data.
+
+Covered invariants include safe deployment configuration/private-path denial; signing/query order/units; read-only connection success/error/schema handling; credential encryption/nonreflection; session/CSRF/origin/owner boundaries; actual-field mapping; no fake market fallback; exact Futures symbols; missing balances/fees/positions; negative/invalid/stale orders; cost-inclusive funds; loss/cap checks; concurrency/idempotency across restart; disconnect races; persistent emergency stop; disabled mutations/withdrawals/transfers; no signal execution; chronology/gaps/no-look-ahead backtesting; and audit tamper detection. Added cases cover exact ticker/aggregate/health requests, conflicting/raw nested ticker fields, public-only health semantics, independently unavailable sections, bounded/coalesced caches, depth without price availability, full-history links beyond 200 fills, archived wallets, deterministic pagination, exact decimal sums, latest matching research beyond recent windows, persistent index initialization/recovery, and numerical overflow/underflow boundaries.
+
+Use `npm test`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`, `npm run test:coverage`, `npm run check:secrets`, and (with the app running) `npm run test:e2e` to reproduce the local checks. They are **not a substitute for actual account verification**.
+
+### Recorded local results — 19 October 2026
+
+- **166/166** unit/HTTP integration tests passed across seven files, including 46 added in this continuation; the coverage run also passed. Instrumented backend modules: 92.49% statements, 87.20% branches, 92.88% lines. This is not frontend or bootstrap coverage.
+- **12/12** Playwright cases passed: one actual anonymous preview smoke/private-path check, and eleven explicitly scoped synthetic browser workflows. They cover masked/cleared credentials, lock/disconnect, reviewed paper execution, applied-pair signed reads, signal-only prefill, blocked live opt-in, emergency stop, the entire request audit, mobile navigation/overflow, conflicting public ticker fields/health isolation, decision/fill pagination with archived wallet provenance, explicit-scope JSON download, journal clearing/export lockout, and delayed research-history responses.
+- Typecheck, production build, formatting check, working-tree secret safeguard, and Git whitespace checks passed. The safeguard is heuristic, not proof that any arbitrary file can never contain a secret.
+- Production-dependency audit (`npm audit --omit=dev`) reported zero known advisories at this check; this is not a security certification.
+- Isolated production-bundle smoke passed: built assets, no Vite client, production script CSP, Secure/HttpOnly/SameSite cookie attributes, owner-locked account/journal/research APIs, paper-only health, the updated collection inventory, and eleven denied private paths. Its synthetic configuration was removed from service after the check.
+- A GitHub Actions verification workflow is included but has not been run in this session.
+- Interactive owner setup was exercised through a temporary pseudo-terminal: input remained hidden, `.env` data-directory configuration worked, the generated hash actually verified, files were private, and a missing vault key was not replaced. The shared preview's owner was **not** initialized.
+- Re-running the inventory against the supplied collection confirmed its original pinned source hash. The three newly implemented public-read dispositions and the ticker conflict finding are reflected in the sanitized audit; repeat generation reproduces that current artifact.
+
+No real account test or live order was performed. This sandbox's outbound host allowlist does not include the documented exchange hosts, and no user key/secret was provided. Exchange-facing end-to-end acceptance must be performed from an appropriately secured/whitelisted backend with outbound access; missing collection contracts must still stay unavailable there.
