+# Security model and operating limits
+
+## Scope
+
+This is a **single-owner** workspace for your own secured machine/server, not a multi-tenant exchange service. It is intentionally incapable of outbound exchange mutations. Do not expose the development server as a production service. The preview is read-only until private owner setup.
+
+No software guarantee can remove cryptocurrency market risk. This implementation also cannot claim live-trading readiness: the supplied collection omits essential contracts.
+
+## Credentials
+
+- New API credentials enter through masked, write-only inputs after owner authentication and an HTTPS/localhost check.
+- Like any browser form, the value necessarily exists transiently in the input and outbound request you submit. It is cleared immediately; the server **never sends it back**, includes it in HTML, puts it in browser storage, or logs it. Browser developer tools on your own device can inspect your own request; TLS is essential.
+- No credential reveal/copy endpoint exists. The displayed key is an opaque mask, not the actual key or secret.
+- AES-256-GCM with a fresh 12-byte IV, authenticated version-specific additional data, and a 16-byte authentication tag protects the credential record at rest.
+- The master key is 32 bytes. Production requires backend secret-manager injection via `DARKDEVIL_MASTER_KEY`. It is never a frontend/Vite variable.
+- Local development generates `.runtime/master.key` with mode `0600`. The vault, owner hash, and database are private backend files; the directory is `0700`, files `0600`, process umask `077`. Disk-level access to both local vault and local key defeats encryption: local file permissions are not a substitute for a production secret manager.
+- Vault writes use a private, randomly named temporary file and atomic rename. Disconnect unlinks the encrypted record and aborts active account reads. Unlinking is **not** a physical secure erase guarantee on SSDs, snapshots, or backups. Revoke compromised keys directly in ZebPay.
+- A missing local key beside an existing encrypted vault is an error, never permission to generate a new key. Canonical 32-byte base64 keys and owner hash formats are validated. Source/static/ancestor data-directory locations are rejected before writing.
+- Runtime files, `.env` files, databases, raw Postman exports, logs, and generated artifacts are ignored by Git. No real account credentials were supplied or added to this repository.
+- JavaScript strings cannot be reliably zeroized. API credentials are decrypted only on the backend for supported reads; plaintext buffers are zeroed when practical, but this is not a hardened-memory/hardware-enclave implementation.
+
+## Owner and browser boundary
+
+- Owner setup happens only in an interactive local terminal. The app never offers public first-user registration or remote owner-password reset.
+- Passwords are stored as salted scrypt hashes; comparison uses constant-time byte comparison. No plaintext password is stored.
+- Server-side, random 256-bit session IDs; rotated session/CSRF token at login. HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict cookies; Secure `__Host-` cookies on HTTPS.
+- Sessions expire after 30 minutes idle / 8 hours absolute, and are invalidated by server restart. Locking the workspace aborts private reads and requires saved credentials to be verified again.
+- Strict same-origin checks, CSRF tokens, JSON-only unsafe methods, input/body-size limits, login/API rate limits, and no cross-origin API access.
+- Production requires an exact HTTPS `DARKDEVIL_PUBLIC_ORIGIN`. Deployment must use **exactly one trusted reverse proxy**, with inbound access to the backend restricted appropriately; Express trusts one proxy hop. Do not expose the backend behind an untrusted chain or trust arbitrary forwarded headers.
+- Content security policy; no telemetry, remote fonts, session replay, or third-party chart scripts. Preview framing is limited to self/Arena/e2b origins. Use a stricter frame-ancestors list on a private standalone deployment if desired.
+- A private-path guard runs before both dev and production static/SPA handlers. Dev Vite also denies runtime files, backend/test sources, raw Postman exports, `.env`, `.git`, certificates/keys, and databases. Production serves only `dist/client`, never the repository root. Late owner-request responses cannot reveal workspace account data after the UI is locked.
+- No response contains raw upstream error text or arbitrary exchange JSON. Schema-invalid responses fail closed; errors use curated messages. HTTP 403 is labeled permission missing, but its exact account/whitelist cause is not guessed.
+
+**Operator responsibility:** disable request bodies/headers/cookies in proxy, load-balancer, APM, crash, and session-replay logs. Restrict the deployment and secret-manager account. Do not enter exchange credentials on an untrusted public demo, device, extension, or network.
+
+## Exchange transport
+
+- Only fixed, source-pinned **HTTPS GET** operations to `www.zebapi.com` and `futuresbe.zebpay.com` exist. No user-controlled base URL, generic proxy, or exchange mutation transport.
+- Each allowed operation is traced to the audited collection request and a concrete originalRequest or defined variable.
+- Private signing applies only to verified Spot GET requests, using millisecond timestamps and the documented query bytes/HMAC-SHA256 hex headers.
+- Public Futures calls never attach Spot credentials. Ticker/aggregate reads validate exact returned symbols against public metadata; malformed, cross-symbol, or unavailable sections fail independently. A literal public health `OK` cannot authenticate a key. Snapshots have a bounded 15-second cache and four distinct in-flight load slots; no inferred backfill or automatic private retry. Authenticated Futures calls are not implemented.
+- Redirects are rejected. Reads have an 8-second timeout, bounded response size, explicit schema validation, and no private automatic retry.
+- Connection generations plus abort controllers prevent disconnected/superseded reads or a late verification response from restoring access. A process restart starts saved credentials unverified.
+- HTTP 200 alone does not establish Connected: the pending-orders response must match the collection's success envelope and order-array schema.
+- Read access does not prove trading permission, actual identity, IP-whitelist status, or current account funds. There is no order-placement permission probe.
+
+## Execution boundaries
+
+### Paper
+
+Only manual, positive base-asset quantities for exact, observed **INR Spot** markets are accepted. Twelve-decimal input precision is an **application simulation constraint**, not an assumed exchange lot size. Long-only, market simulations; no margin, shorts, leverage, limit matching, partial fills, or Futures simulation.
+
+The engine has a public-market service, **not a private exchange-order adapter**. It validates the mode/schema, positive quantity, supported exact market, fresh local quote, full-portfolio valuation, virtual funds/assets, maximum notional, daily-loss reference, and projected cost impact. SQLite transactions protect accounting/idempotency; the kill switch and audit integrity are checked before quote lookup and again before commit.
+
+UUID-based request IDs and canonical fingerprints are persistent. The same payload/request ID replays its recorded result. Conflicting ID reuse and identical orders within 30 seconds are rejected. Local request-status lookup reconciles an unconfirmed paper response without another fill.
+
+Fees and slippage are explicitly configured **assumptions**, not parsed real ZebPay costs. The reference is the received public `market` price, not a guaranteed executable book quote. No exchange timestamp is invented for Spot market data; local receipt freshness cannot prove that an upstream exchange price itself is fresh.
+
+Daily loss is simulated mark-to-market relative to the first fresh valuation in the UTC day; it includes fees and adverse slippage. A new day requires a fresh valuation. A missing held-asset price means no current equity/P&L and no new simulation. Resetting the virtual portfolio is an explicit local-only operation with a typed confirmation; old fills and audit records remain archived.
+
+### Live
+
+`liveEnabled` is always false. There is no environment/browser override. An opt-in UI requires risk acknowledgment, then the backend refuses activation with the missing-contract explanation. Four Spot serializers and the POST signing recipe are offline-only utilities with tests, not a sending path.
+
+Real balances, Spot trading filters, verified costs/permissions, real daily-loss valuation, DELETE signing, and unambiguous Futures private authentication cannot be checked from this collection. It would be unsafe to invent these. No live orders, cancellations, margin/leverage changes, withdrawals, or transfers are sent.
+
+Read-only reconciliation of a **known** Spot ID queries documented pending and Complete filters. Missing status is unresolved, not permission to resubmit. Without a verified client-order ID, the app cannot safely correlate a hypothetical unknown placement outcome; this is another reason not to add a live sender casually.
+
+### Emergency stop
+
+The stop is latched persistently and blocks new simulations before and after quote validation. It aborts authenticated reads and leaves credentials saved-but-unverified. A separate typed reset is required. Reset never enables live execution.
+
+**It cannot cancel existing exchange orders or guarantee that orders placed outside this app stop executing.** Manage existing orders directly in ZebPay. The interface repeats this warning.
+
+## Persistence, auditing, backups
+
+- Single-instance SQLite, WAL, full synchronous commits, private data directory. Use encrypted disks/backups and least-privilege filesystem/secret-manager access.
+- Logs store only allowlisted noncredential metadata. Audit entries are linked with HMAC-SHA256 under a domain-separated key derived from the master key; verified at startup and before paper execution.
+- This detects edits within the retained local chain but is **not immutable or externally anchored**. An attacker controlling the database/key, or truncating/deleting an entire suffix/database, is outside that guarantee. No compliance-grade nonrepudiation is claimed.
+- Keep the master key separate from encrypted data backups; do not rotate it by overwriting the file/env key. This version has no in-place key-rotation workflow. Restore the original key or deliberately disconnect/reinitialize after taking an appropriate backup.
+- Decision execution summaries query the complete persisted local ledger across current/archived wallets. BUY entries have no inferred realized exit outcome; SELL metrics are recorded simulated fill results, not strategy accuracy. Paginated detail reads remain owner-only and cannot submit trades. Financial aggregates use decimal strings, not SQLite floating-point sums.
+- On-screen journal exports contain bounded records, not the entire SQLite database or a complete archival backup. Protect downloaded financial journals as private account information even though credentials are omitted.
+- For a simple manual backup, stop the app first and back up the whole private runtime directory consistently, keeping its matching key separately protected. Copying only a live SQLite main file is not a reliable WAL backup.
+- Unverified network/account behavior remains unverified. Mocked tests demonstrate local contracts and safety invariants, not actual account permissions or exchange execution.
+
+## Before expanding to live trading
+
+Obtain a corrected, complete authoritative collection: exact Spot balance/fee/filter schemas and units; real loss valuation semantics; API-scope/IP introspection or an explicitly reviewed alternative; DELETE signing/response contracts; unknown-order correlation/idempotency; unambiguous Futures auth/nonces/order examples. Audit the changes, implement all server-side checks and reconciliation, threat-model them, and test them independently. Do not remove gates, reuse another exchange's rules, or merely add a `LIVE_ENABLED` environment flag.
